VIEWMODEL.md §4.5: a slider on a number type without a lower bound is E1619 (lower); a sized integer's limits count, the int64 ones do not.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

local record Item {
  count: Int
  top: Int(..=10)
  small: Int8
  level: Int(0..=10)
  rate: Float(0.0..1.0)
}

view Item {
  count { control: slider }
  top { control: slider }
  small { control: slider }
  level { control: slider }
  rate { control: slider }
}
-- findings.txt --
error[E1619]  a/a.canon:12:20
  slider needs both bounds, and Int has no lower bound

error[E1619]  a/a.canon:13:18
  slider needs both bounds, and Int(..=10) has no lower bound

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
